ZERO OS0.9 NETWORK/WIFI INTEGRATION CANDIDATE - ALL FOUR MODES PASS
Date:2026-11-16 UTC

Exact candidate ISO:17776640 bytes
SHA256:bfcff263a4df655f9eb1760dd70de1538304a9902776bced8fbd89c23062e3c6
Path:build/network-candidate.qby3zn9o/zero.iso
This is an integration candidate, not the final release. The requested default
in-guest compiler bundle is still a separate pending integration at this point.

Actual QEMU pc/TCG runs:BIOS64,BIOS32(-lm,-pae),AMD64 OVMF,IA32 OVMF(-lm).
All use128MiB RAM,standardVGA1920x1080 and emulated AMD PCnet with user NAT.
No data disks are attached. All four VMs exited and the ISO hash stayed unchanged.

Each run independently verifies:
- Actual DHCP Discover/Offer/Request/ACK exchange before ANY terminal input.
  The later net command only reads state. BIOS read-only memory also confirms
  state4,IP10.0.2.15,mask255.255.255.0,gateway10.0.2.2,DNS10.0.2.3.
- Native1920x1080 framebuffer screenshots.
- pause2 stops computation without stopping the network worker. A QMP cable
  disconnect clears all published IPv4 configuration; reconnect triggers a
  second complete DHCP exchange automatically, with no reconnect command.
- HTTP/1.0 200 from an independent host-only fixture while computation remains
  paused. The real guest TCP client sends GET and receives the fixture marker.
- Real public DNS resolution of10.0.2.2.nip.io, followed by another actual HTTP
  fetch to the LOCAL fixture through that resolved address. This is DNS plus
  local HTTP evidence, not a claim of public Internet HTTP reachability.
- The production wifi command opens the native fullscreen modal and truthfully
  reports no PCI wireless adapter. Real PS/2 Up/Down,F1,F5,q and Enter do not
  change the modal or leak q into terminal input; Escape restores the terminal.
  The two terminal sessions and tile layout remain intact. BIOS snapshots
  confirm production marker0,network-count0,correct error phase and all64
  password bytes zero before/after closure.
- Independently decoded PCAP has no invalid guest IPv4/TCP checksums.
  Each mode contains8 DHCP messages(two complete exchanges),2 DNS packets and
  2 real HTTP GET requests. Host fixture logs confirm all8 requested paths.

Visible evidence
bios64/wifi-no-adapter.png and dns-http-response.png were visually inspected:
legible text, correct FullHD rendering, clear status, no frame corruption.
All four modes' no-adapter modal images have identical RGB pixel hashes;
wifi-modal-parity.json records that independent comparison. The modal currently
shows000WINDOWS in its header although the two underlying sessions survive;
this cosmetic label issue was reported to the root for the final integration.

Environment and limits
external-http-host-probe.json records that host TCP toexample.com:80 returns
ENETUNREACH. Public Internet HTTP is therefore not claimed by this run.
Native VirtualBox and physical hardware were not tested. QEMU has no native
WiFi radio; PCnet/NAT traffic is Ethernet. Real wireless association, WPA2,
SSID scans and passwords are not exercised by these four VMs. Separate hosted
WiFi UI fixtures are explicitly labelled SIMULATION/NO RADIO/NO PACKETS.

Historical failure
Earlier candidate39980079 completed automatic DHCP on all four architectures,
but its registered net command emitted no status because NET COMMANDS had been
removed by another integration region refresh. Root corrected the marker
placement and checked all source integrations before building this candidate.
That earlier failed run is preserved separately and is not final success data.

Evidence
matrix.json; per-mode result.json,actions.jsonl,serial transcripts,readonly
state JSON,packet summaries and nativePNG captures. RawPCAP,PPM,memory dumps,
pflash variables and sockets are internal test artifacts. No user disk was
read,written,formatted or attached by this task.
